# Lock the dist-kernel to the 7.2.x series as a whole; no per-release names.
# ::gentoo dropped every 7.2.x ebuild, so an unlocked @world installs the 6.18.63
# LTS downgrade and then fails in prepare: this machine carries out-of-tree amdgpu
# patches under /etc/portage/patches/sys-kernel/gentoo-kernel/, and 0002 there
# targets dc_dmub_srv_handle_failure(), which does not exist before 7.x. Verified
# on a tree prepared exactly like the ebuild (base + patch-6.18.63 + gentoo
# patchset): 0001, 0003 and 0004 apply, 0002 fails. On 7.3.4 it is 0001 that
# fails, so no released series takes all four except the 7.2.x we run.
# The next 7.2.x ebuild to land becomes selectable on its own. This also covers
# 6.18.33 and 6.18.33_p1, whose upstream sources changed size without
# regenerated manifests.
# chihiro is Intel and has no such patches, so it tracks kernels normally.
<sys-kernel/gentoo-kernel-7.2
>=sys-kernel/gentoo-kernel-7.3
<virtual/dist-kernel-7.2
>=virtual/dist-kernel-7.3
{{- end }}

